   "lane": "paritok",
   "answer": "Based on the codebase analysis, when you call `requests.get()` and data flows down to the socket, the request hand-off proceeds through the following classes and methods:\n\n1. **`requests.api` (`requests.get`)**: \n   - `requests.get()` calls `requests.api.request('get', url, **kwargs)` (`src/requests/api.py`).\n   - This instantiates a `requests.sessions.Session` and delegates to its `request()` method (`src/requests/api.py`).\n\n2. **`requests.sessions.Session`**:\n   - `Session.request()` builds a `Request` object, calls `.prepare()` on it to get a `PreparedRequest`, and handles parameters, headers, cookies, and authentication (`src/requests/sessions.py`).\n   - It then invokes `Session.send(prep, **send_kwargs)` (`src/requests/sessions.py`).\n\n3. **`requests.adapters.BaseAdapter` / `HTTPAdapter`**:\n   - `Session.send()` retrieves the appropriate connection adapter for the URL scheme (typically an instance of `requests.adapters.HTTPAdapter`) and calls `adapter.send(request, **kwargs)` (`src/requests/sessions.py` and `src/requests/adapters.py`).\n\n4. **`urllib3` Connection Pool and Connection Classes**:\n   - `HTTPAdapter.send()` uses a `urllib3` connection pool manager to get a connection object (typically `urllib3.connectionpool.HTTPConnectionPool` / `HTTPSConnectionPool` and `urllib3.connection.HTTPConnection` / `HTTPSConnection`).\n   - The connection eventually hands off the HTTP request bytes to the underlying Python standard library socket (`socket.socket`) via `sock.sendall()` or equivalent transport mechanisms within `urllib3`.",
